'''Drake's Dragonite''' (Japanese: '''ユウジのカイリュー''' ''Yūji's Kairyu'') is {{OBP|Drake|Orange League}}'s main Pokémon in {{aniseries|OS}}. Drake keeps {{p|Dragonite}}'s {{i|Poké Ball}} around his neck.

==In animation==
===''Pokémon the Series''===
===={{aniseries|OS}}====
[[File:Drake and Dragonite.png|left|thumb|220px|Dragonite and Drake]]
Dragonite first appeared in ''[[EP111|Hello, Pummelo!]]'', when it was seen flying around [[Pummelo Island]]. Later, when {{TRT}} tried to steal Dragonite, they were sent blasting off from its {{m|Hyper Beam}} attack.

In ''[[EP112|Enter The Dragonite]]'', Drake used Dragonite as his final Pokémon in his [[Full Battle]] against {{Ash}}. It was shown to be a very strong battler. With its impressive speed and power, it was able to take out {{AP|Charizard}}, {{AP|Squirtle}}, and {{AP|Tauros}}, although all three managed to land at least one blow on Dragonite before they fainted. Even though it fought three of Ash's Pokémon, it was still able to defeat Team Rocket when they tried another attempt at capturing it when it was tired out. 

It then had to battle {{AP|Pikachu}} in the last round of the match. Despite being tired out from the previous battles, it managed to put up a good fight against Pikachu, but, after a fierce battle, it was defeated by Pikachu's use of a {{m|Thunder}} attack while positioned on Dragonite's head, making Ash an Honored Trainer of the [[Orange League]].

===Personality and characteristics===
Drake's Dragonite is truly a force to be reckoned with. Drake holds his Dragonite in high regard, even keeping a modeled statue of it and its {{i|Poké Ball}}  around his neck, a testament to their bond. This particular Dragonite is renowned for its unyielding stamina and incredible resilience, consistently overpowering numerous trainers before its  clash with Ash. It's a testament to its indomitable spirit that, even after a grueling battle against four of Ash's Pokémon, including a tough struggle against Charizard, Dragonite still possessed the might to defeat half of Ash's team. Despite being tired from its prior victories, Dragonite enough fourth Pokémon to faced [[Ash's Pikachu]], putting up a fierce battle before finally being defeated by a strategic Thunder attack.

